# halfcenter v57d -- THE DRIVE SWEEP. A candidate window, NOT yet a clock.
# 2026-09-18. Gated on verify PASS (hash ad96f882becbee92, 22 experiments, 7.6 min).
#
# drive140 (tonic 1.40, jump 1.00, hc 0.60, tau 167) reaches anti-phase -0.555 with
# 0/12 seeds degenerate, and it PASSES the drift check that killed the previous
# positive: halves -0.554 / -0.556 against -0.555 whole, i.e. identical. Rate 6.38 Hz
# (ctrl 4.93), duty 0.57. The interaction is -97.1 SE against the matched-drive
# control.
#
# THE SE OF 0.000 IS NOT THE DEGENERATE GUARD. That guard returns exactly 0.0; this
# is a computed correlation all twelve seeds agree on to three decimals, which is
# what a strongly locked, seed-independent limit cycle looks like.
#
# TWO DOUBTS REMAIN, AND NEITHER IS SETTLED BY THIS RUN:
#
# 1. PERIOD vs RESONANCE. Every arm of every run so far peaks at 2.5-3.5 Hz, which is
#    the band the pre-existing damped resonance already occupies:
#      drive 0.00 3.15 Hz | 0.30 2.48 | 0.50 2.71 | 0.70 2.96 | 0.85 2.85 |
#      1.00 3.35 | 1.40 3.46
#    Period is PROPORTIONAL to tau_a for a relaxation oscillator, so the exponent must
#    be ~1.0. This run held tau at 167 ms and cannot test it. adaptclock measured
#    +0.226 and the released-jump run -0.121.
#
# 2. POPULATION vs PER-NEURON. Drive 1.40 is 2.2x the 0.645 spike threshold, so each
#    neuron can relaxation-oscillate ALONE -- fire, fatigue, shut off, recover -- which
#    would give anti-phase between halves with no population competition at all. The
#    rate sd (6.765) EXCEEDS the mean (6.38), so firing is strongly bursty.
#    Discriminator: within a half, neurons should be POSITIVELY correlated with each
#    other under a population half-center and not under per-neuron bursting. Not
#    measured here.
#
# AND THE PROFILE IS NOT SHPIRO'S WINDOW SHAPE:
#   drive 0.00 11/12 deg VOID | 0.30 3/12 VOID | 0.50 0/12 anti 0.000 |
#   0.70 12/12 settled | 0.85 11/12 settled | 1.00 12/12 settled | 1.40 0/12 -0.555
# A winner-take-all plateau from 0.70 to 1.00 with the effect appearing only at the
# TOP arm, so the sweep is one-sided and the window's upper edge is unmeasured.
#
# THE FOLLOW-UP IS RUNNING: tau swept 83/167/250/333 AT drive 1.40 (the clock test),
# both singles at that same drive rather than at 0.85, a within-half coherence
# readout, and drive 2.00 to probe above the window. The verdict is now GATED on the
# exponent: below 0.60 it prints "not a clock" and returns false.
