  --- the reading ---
  THE TWO HALVES TAKE TURNS. `drive140` reaches anti-phase -0.555, beating BOTH of
  its own singles by at least 3 SE -- so it is the COMBINATION and not
  either ingredient, which is Matsuoka's prediction and the interaction this
  run pre-registered.
  A resonance moves both halves TOGETHER, so this cannot be the 3 Hz ring
  being re-measured -- the failure that killed adaptclock.
  THIS RUN DOES NOT SWEEP tau, SO IT CANNOT CALL THIS A CLOCK. It locates a
  candidate WINDOW on the drive axis; whether the period tracks tau_a is the
  NEXT run, at this drive. adaptclock measured +0.226 and the released-jump
  run -0.121, against the ~1.000 a relaxation oscillator requires.
